  "answer": "This feature has been requested before, many times. It isn't available in Awake today. Awake has no list of apps that keep the PC awake. The main request is PowerToys#32467, which is still open. It asks for an app list in Awake, and the maintainer is weighing it. He is worried about the cost of polling running processes and about Awake growing too complex. A sketch of a 'Watcher' mode has been discussed. Similar requests are #14027 and #32787. To help, add a thumbs-up and your use case to #32467. In the meantime, Awake's command-line options can tie it to a process. Use `--pid`, or `--use-parent-id` when launching the app from a script. Another option is a third-party tool that watches for running processes."
 },
